interactive store right after creating it and hooks the headless store
to the same signal. Both wirings now exist; an annulment control that
turns the REPL subscription into a no-op drops exactly its test.

UDS C: the client and receipts module of chunk-qcy58j4w.js lands in
udsClient.ts, with the live session registry and the peer loop guard
it needs. The pool left type errors that its own verify did not run
tsc for; fixed here: the former-name guard narrows to its checked
shape, recordInPidDomain asks only for the fields it reads, the guard
bucket receives the clock it calls, and RegistryStorage is re-exported
for the client. THYROX_CODE_HARBOR_KITE_PACING_OFF is declared.

ADR-THYROX-006 1.1.0, phases R1 and R2. The memory adapter serves a
single proxy; the Redis one runs on Bun.RedisClient and passes the
same contract against an ephemeral redis-server on a Unix socket.
The toolchain gains thyrox_toolchain_require_redis, opt-in and
re-checking the binary.

openSharedStateStore picks Redis when THYROX_REDIS_URL is set and
memory otherwise. When Redis fails mid-operation it degrades to
memory once, with a warning, and stays there. Annulling that
fallback drops exactly its two cases.

The redis contract resolves redis-server through
thyrox_toolchain_require_redis instead of PATH, so the opt-in and the
binary re-check govern the test as they govern every consumer.

